{"study_accession":"PRJNA1216658","secondary_study_accession":"SRP560470","title":"Endogenous retroviruses promote aberrant T cell differentiation in systemic lupus erythematosus via the RIG-I pathway [naïve]","description":"The dysregulated differentiation of T lymphocytes play an important role in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE). However, the underlying mechanism remains unclear. Our findings reveal many overexpressed HERVs in CD4+ T cells from SLE patients. To investigate the role of dsRNA/RIG-I pathway in CD4+ T cell differentiation, RNA-seq was performed in CD3 and CD28 antibodies activated naive CD4+ T cells transfected with poly(I:C). The expression profiles of genes related to the effector T cell differentiation reveal that dsRNAs induced the activation of the RIG-I signaling pathway plays important roles in aberrant differentiation of T cells. Overall design: mRNA prifules of naive CD4+T cells of HCs with poly(I:C) treatment","pubmed":"40992212","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN46439781","study_accession":"PRJNA1216658","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"naive_poly_4","description":"naive_poly_4","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8762616","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-12-21","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_type","CD4+T cells"],["treatment","poly"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR32156990","experiment_accession":"SRX27502537","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":20281087,"base_count":6084326100,"first_public":"2025-12-21","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8762616: naive_poly_4 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN46439782","study_accession":"PRJNA1216658","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"naive_poly_3","description":"naive_poly_3